1.7 class: Browser
==================

   • extends: EventEmitter
     (https://nodejs.org/api/events.html#events_class_eventemitter)

A Browser is created when Puppeteer connects to a Chromium instance,
either through *note ‘puppeteer.launch’: #puppeteerlaunchoptions. or
*note ‘puppeteer.connect’: #puppeteerconnectoptions.

An example of using a *note Browser: #class-browser. to create a *note
Page: #class-page.:

const puppeteer = require('puppeteer');

puppeteer.launch().then(async browser => {
  const page = await browser.newPage();
  await page.goto('https://example.com');
  await browser.close();
});

An example of disconnecting from and reconnecting to a *note Browser:
#class-browser.:

const puppeteer = require('puppeteer');

puppeteer.launch().then(async browser => {
  // Store the endpoint to be able to reconnect to Chromium
  const browserWSEndpoint = browser.wsEndpoint();
  // Disconnect puppeteer from Chromium
  browser.disconnect();

  // Use the endpoint to reestablish a connection
  const browser2 = await puppeteer.connect({browserWSEndpoint});
  // Close Chromium
  await browser2.close();
});

