The only difference between ‘worker.evaluate’ and
‘worker.evaluateHandle’ is that ‘worker.evaluateHandle’ returns in-page
object (JSHandle).

If the function passed to the ‘worker.evaluateHandle’ returns a Promise
(https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Promise),
then ‘worker.evaluateHandle’ would wait for the promise to resolve and
return its value.

