1.12.4 keyboard.type(text[, options])
-------------------------------------

   • ‘text’ <string
     (https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Data_structures#String_type)>
     A text to type into a focused element.
   • ‘options’ <Object
     (https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Object)>
        • ‘delay’ <number
          (https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Data_structures#Number_type)>
          Time to wait between key presses in milliseconds.  Defaults to
          0.

   • returns: <Promise
     (https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Promise)>

Sends a ‘keydown’, ‘keypress’/‘input’, and ‘keyup’ event for each
character in the text.

To press a special key, like ‘Control’ or ‘ArrowDown’, use *note
‘keyboard.press’: #keyboardpresskey-options.

page.keyboard.type('Hello'); // Types instantly
page.keyboard.type('World', {delay: 100}); // Types slower, like a user

     *NOTE* Modifier keys DO NOT effect ‘keyboard.type’.  Holding down
     ‘Shift’ will not type the text in upper case.


